On Wed, 8 Nov 2006, azgor wrote:
>
> This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
> freenode.net. Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.
>
> [1]: The amulet of Yendor should slowly increase in weight after you
> first pick it up, kind of like the one ring did for Frodo. Should make
> Astral a bit more challenging. --scwizard

   Horribly unbalancing in the "ha ha, you can't win" sense, if the
increase isn't capped at some reasonable point... but then you might
as well just make the Amulet really heavy to begin with... but that
would be stupid. So, no.

> [2]: Applying the Scepter of Might to a rock enchants it. Only for
> caveman of course. --SpeedEvil

   Makes no sense. Also, can you even (a)pply the Scepter /to/ things
in the first place?
   However, if we're willing to stretch the definition of "caveman" a
little, and insert obscure "2001" references, I suggest that (F)ighting
downward while wielding a club and standing over a dead quadruped
should exercise intelligence. :)

   Strangely, (F)ighting downward, or upward, or at oneself, doesn't
seem to work (in 3.4.3 vanilla, on MS-DOS). It just gives me the
"cmdassist" help screen. This might not be a bug per se, but it's
certainly strange that there aren't YAFMs for those three directions
instead.

> [6]: (A)pplying a camera should light up a room/radius temporarily.
> --ekiM

   Well, it sort-of does. But as someone recently mentioned in the Grue
thread, you can't see anything that was momentarily lit up by the flash.
I'd like to see this fixed --- maybe the given direction should be lit
up, and then the game pauses to let you examine the screen, and after you
hit a key to continue, the area becomes dark again and the game resumes.
(In fact, the "hit a key to continue" part could be a natural consequence
of a "--more--" prompt.)

> [8]: If you die by choking on an artifact weapon, you should get
> "choked on Magicbane" instead of "choked on a Magicbane".
> --Dentarthurdent_

   This sounds more like a bug report than a YANI. Did you report it?

> [9]: when polymorphed into a flying monster, you ought to be able to
> reach the bottom of a pit. --Dentarthurdent_

   You ought to be able to reach the bottom of a pit in any event, unless
you're levitating. There already exist patches for descending into pits
via '>', or #sitting on the edge of the pit, or whatever; I think some
of these good ideas are coming in the next version, too.

> [14]: You should be able to bless/curse things on the ground by pouring
> (un)holy water on them. --Dentarthurdent_

   kundor asks what this is good for. I answer: When there's a loadstone
on the ground and you have some water in your inventory, but you don't
know if the water is blessed or not. And for some reason you want to
pick up the loadstone. Maybe?
   Anyway, IIRC, my "splash patch" lets you throw holy water to bless
things with some middling-to-low chance.

-Arthur


